# Mausam Sense — environment variables
#
# The app works with ZERO configuration: Open-Meteo (weather, air quality,
# geocoding) is a keyless public API and is used directly from the browser.
#
# IMD (India Meteorological Department) public APIs require an API key that
# must be requested from IMD (api.imd.gov.in). Without a key, the app shows
# an explicit "official warnings unavailable" state and never fabricates
# official-looking warnings.
#
# In Vite, only variables prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the browser.
# An IMD key here IS visible to end users — only use it for hackathon/demo
# purposes, never for a secrets-bearing production deployment (proxy it
# through a backend instead).

# Optional: issued IMD API key (enables official warnings / advisories)
VITE_IMD_API_KEY=

# Optional: IMD district id (numeric id used by IMD's districtwarning endpoint).
# Required together with the key above; IMD identifies districts by id, not name.
VITE_IMD_DISTRICT_ID=

# Optional: base URL of the Mausam Sense ML backend (FastAPI) used by the
# "Rainfall Intelligence" dashboard panel (prediction / verification /
# metrics). Defaults to http://localhost:8000 when unset. The backend is a
# separate deployment from this static site — see backend/README.md for CORS
# and deployment notes. No secrets belong here; the ML API is read-only.
VITE_ML_API_BASE=
